Section 1: Mission Context & Execution EnvironmentObjective: Construct an internal web application to replace ad-hoc chat and spreadsheet workflows for coordinating operational tasks, incident resolutions, and compliance requests across multiple teams.   Agent Directives: Prioritize engineering judgment, data consistency, and system correctness over a high feature count or decorative UI. The architecture must be robust enough to handle concurrent usage, stale data, and rapid system updates.   Environment Constraints:The entire application infrastructure (backend, frontend, database, and async workers) must initialize seamlessly via a single docker-compose up command for reviewer accessibility.   A relational database (PostgreSQL is highly recommended) must be used to leverage ACID transactions, row-level locks, constraints, and indexing.   The system must be designed for scale: assume tens of thousands of active work items and a growing history. All data lists must utilize server-side cursor pagination, filtering, and search. Never load complete datasets into browser memory.   Scope Exclusions (Do Not Build): To ensure bug-free delivery of critical components, explicitly exclude user registration flows (use database seeding instead), Single Sign-On (SSO), email delivery, file attachments, real-time WebSockets (rely on TanStack Query refetching), and mobile applications.   